WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:09.347
A rate compares two different kinds of things, like kilometres and hours. A unit rate tells us the amount for just one.

00:09.797 --> 00:16.484
To find the unit rate, divide. One hundred fifty kilometres divided by three hours.

00:16.934 --> 00:20.417
So the rate is fifty kilometres for each hour.

00:20.867 --> 00:26.928
Now we can use it. How far in five hours? Multiply the unit rate by five.

00:27.378 --> 00:33.856
Unit rates also help us compare. The smaller price for one item is the better buy.
